{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slideIndex":2,"text":"The manipulated quantity is gallery prevalence: the proportion of gallery images carrying the target pathology. Gallery size, fitted model, query set, and retrieval depth remain fixed. This isolates prevalence at evaluation time rather than changing training-set balance.\n\nSource: Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx, supplied manuscript. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/jyx0ra1s","slideIndex":3,"layout":{"id":"ly/3yt8jipk","name":"ICAST Content"},"title":"Background and Research Gap","textShapes":3,"backgroundColor":"rgba(250,250,250,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/1cj2d8b6","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":120,"top":0,"width":1040,"height":104.57},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"title","text":"Background and Research Gap","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":48,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#FFFFFF","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/0ba143al","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":57.6,"top":148.8,"width":1164.48,"height":480},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"body","text":"Image retrieval returns similar prior cases for education and reference.\nExisting work studies embeddings, rare diseases and imbalanced galleries.\nChanging examples per class in a balanced index preserves prevalence.\nThis study fixes gallery size and reduces the target share from 5% to 0.5%.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#333333","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/r29obap4","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":1173.52,"top":23.04,"width":58.48,"height":58.48},"name":"Slide Number","placeholder":"slideNumber","text":"4","geometry":"ellipse","fillColor":"#FFFFFF","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#0B2545","bold":true,"alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/jyx0ra1s","slideIndex":3,"text":"Related work motivates the protocol rather than providing directly comparable metric values. Denner et al. [1] compared representations and varied indexed support while keeping classes balanced. SISH [2] and volumetric retrieval [4] examine rare or imbalanced settings. The reviewed work did not isolate a controlled multi-level prevalence reduction while holding queries and representations fixed. This is a narrative, non-systematic review.\n\nSource: Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx, supplied manuscript. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
