{"kind":"image","id":"im/ep4v69gn","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":130,"top":120,"width":1020,"height":565},"fit":"contain","name":"","alt":"Original manuscript Figure 2 showing fixed 200-query sets, four prevalence levels and five gallery samples, with exact gallery composition."}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/x8f69ofe","slideIndex":5,"text":"Original Figure 2 from the supplied manuscript. Three target pathologies: cardiomegaly, emphysema and pneumothorax. Each has 200 fixed queries. Every gallery contains 20,000 images with 1,000, 400, 200 or 100 relevant cases. Three non-target pathology distractors each contribute 400 images. Five seeds per target and prevalence yield 60 galleries. All six models use the same manifests. Tuberculosis was excluded as a target after a source-bias audit but remained a 2% distractor.\n\nSource: Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx, supplied manuscript. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
