{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/udsvah03","slideIndex":8,"text":"SwAV-SupCon ranked first in mean P@10 in all 12 conditions. Its advantage over SwAV-CLS survived global correction in 10 of 12 planned comparisons. The exceptions were cardiomegaly at 0.5% and 1%. At 0.5%, SupCon versus CLS P@10: cardiomegaly 0.0163 versus 0.0133 (adjusted p > 0.99), emphysema 0.0335 versus 0.0175 (p = 5.34 × 10^-7), pneumothorax 0.0660 versus 0.0446 (p = 3.17 × 10^-6). Enrichment factors 3.26, 6.70 and 13.20 divide the leading mean by the random expectation of 0.005. Low absolute precision limits practical interpretation. Results are conditional on one fitted checkpoint per learned condition and objective-specific checkpoint selection.\n\nSource: Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx, supplied manuscript. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/m90b6t0r","slideIndex":9,"layout":{"id":"ly/3yt8jipk","name":"ICAST Content"},"title":"Conclusion and Future Work","textShapes":3,"backgroundColor":"rgba(250,250,250,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/xc3mho32","slideIndex":9,"position":{"left":120,"top":0,"width":1040,"height":104.57},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"title","text":"Conclusion and Future Work","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":48,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#FFFFFF","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/cbu58j2h","slideIndex":9,"position":{"left":57.6,"top":148.8,"width":1164.48,"height":480},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"body","text":"Conclusion\nLower target prevalence substantially reduces retrieval quality.\nSwAV-SupCon leads here, but rare-case precision remains limited.\nLimits\nOne training run, imperfect labels and cross-source confounding.\nFuture work\nRepeat training, strengthen source controls and assess clinical relevance.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#0B2545","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/25kv2h0f","slideIndex":9,"position":{"left":1173.52,"top":23.04,"width":58.48,"height":58.48},"name":"Slide Number","placeholder":"slideNumber","text":"10","geometry":"ellipse","fillColor":"#FFFFFF","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#0B2545","bold":true,"alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/m90b6t0r","slideIndex":9,"text":"Additional limitations: every model uses ResNet-50, external labels are not exhaustive, SIIM patient uniqueness cannot be verified, and no clinician assessed relevance. Pneumothorax source is aligned with query-gallery role, so the result is not a source-controlled estimate of pathology-specific similarity. The lowest prevalence still has 100 relevant images, and larger approximate indexes were not evaluated. No study measured diagnostic benefit. Future work should test additional architectures, lower relevant-case counts and clinically assessed relevance.\n\nSource: Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx, supplied manuscript. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
